{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.CechKummerSurface","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CechKummerSurface","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.CechColimitConverse","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.CechChernClass"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.bring_kummer_trivial_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.bring_kummer_trivial_iff","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L202-L209","doc":"**Genus 4 (for example Bring's curve, `χ = 2 − 2·4 = −6`).** The Kummer class\nof the tangent cocycle is trivial iff `n ∣ 6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.exists_nthRoot_on_refinement_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.exists_nthRoot_on_refinement_iff","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L187-L200","doc":"**R3 with the converse (G1b).** On a directed system of covers, `γ` has an\n`n`-th root `η` (a `U(1)`-cocycle with `ηⁿ = γ`) on some finer admissible cover\niff `n ∣ χ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.kummer_class_trivial_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.kummer_class_trivial_iff","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L177-L185","doc":"**R3, conditional.** If `c₁(γ)` has degree `χ`, the Kummer class of `γ` is\ntrivial iff `n ∣ χ`. For `γ` the transition cocycle of the tangent bundle, `χ`\nis the Euler characteristic (Poincaré–Hopf, assumed through `hχ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.KummerSurfaceData.degN_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.KummerSurfaceData.degN_map","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L175-L175","doc":"reduction mod `n` commutes with the degrees ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.KummerSurfaceData.degN_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.KummerSurfaceData.degN_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L171-L171","doc":"the `μₙ` degree vanishes exactly on the trivial class ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.KummerSurfaceData.degN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.KummerSurfaceData.degN","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L169-L169","doc":"degree on `Ȟ²(S, μₙ)` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.KummerSurfaceData.deg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.KummerSurfaceData.deg","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L167-L167","doc":"degree on `Ȟ²(S, ℤ)` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.KummerSurfaceData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.KummerSurfaceData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L164-L164","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.KummerSurfaceData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.KummerSurfaceData","kind":"class","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L158-L175","doc":"**Topological input for a closed oriented surface `S` (hypothesis, not\nproved).** A degree map on `Ȟ²(S, ℤ)`, a degree map on `Ȟ²(S, μₙ)` that detects\nthe trivial class (the injectivity half of `Ȟ²(S, μₙ) ≅ ℤ/n`), and compatibility\nof the two with reduction mod `n`. For a closed oriented surface these follow\nfrom the comparison of Čech and singular cohomology with constant coefficients\nand the orientation class; Mathlib has neither, so they are assumed here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.cechKummer_eq_map_chern","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.cechKummer_eq_map_chern","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L146-L156","doc":"**Kummer relation in the colimit `Ȟ²`.** The obstruction class to an `n`-th\nroot of `γ` is the reduction mod `n` of the Chern class of `γ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.kappaMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.kappaMap","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L136-L139","doc":"Reduction `κ : ℤ → μₙ`, `k ↦ exp(2πik/n)`, as a morphism of presheaves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.chernCocycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.Cech.chernCocycle","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L126-L132","doc":"The Čech Chern cochain `c₁(γ)` (relative to a real lift `ξ`) as a 2-cocycle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.CechH2.map_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.CechH2.map_one","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L110-L113","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.CechH2.map_cechClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.CechH2.map_cechClass","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L107-L108","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.CechH2.map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.CechH2.map","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L98-L105","doc":"**Change of coefficients on the colimit `Ȟ²`.** It is well defined because\npushing forward commutes with refinement (definitionally) and preserves the\ncohomology relation (`TwoCocycle.Rel.map`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.CoverCocycle.map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.CoverCocycle.map","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L94-L96","doc":"Push a cocycle on an admissible cover forward. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.TwoCocycle.Rel.map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.TwoCocycle.Rel.map","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L80-L86","doc":"Cohomologous cocycles push forward to cohomologous cocycles. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.TwoCocycle.one_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.TwoCocycle.one_map","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L75-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.TwoCocycle.map_ev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.TwoCocycle.map_ev","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L71-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.TwoCocycle.map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.TwoCocycle.map","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L63-L69","doc":"Push a 2-cocycle forward along a morphism of presheaves of groups. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.TwoCocycle.ext_cochain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.TwoCocycle.ext_cochain","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechKummerSurface.lean#L58-L61","doc":"Two 2-cocycles with the same underlying cochain are equal. ","signatureChunk":0}]}